Qwen3.8-Flash-Next decode patch 06: advise PLE pages before the decode gather.

vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ngram_embedding.py (needs
flash-next-ttft-01-ple-page-prefetch.patch)

The rows for a token that was just sampled cannot be prefetched, so on a page
cache miss np.take faulted its ~16 table pages in one at a time, 2-4 ms of
NVMe latency on the critical path per affected step. The gather now asks for
all of those pages in one process_madvise(MADV_WILLNEED) call first, so the
reads overlap. Off together with the prefetch thread (VLLM_PLE_PREFETCH=0).

--- a/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ngram_embedding.py
+++ b/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ngram_embedding.py
@@ -610,6 +610,8 @@
 # VLLM_PLE_PREFETCH=0 disables the prefetch.
 
 _PLE_PREFETCH_ENV = "VLLM_PLE_PREFETCH"
+# Gathers up to this many rows (decode batches) advise their pages first.
+_PLE_GATHER_ADVISE_MAX_ROWS = 256
 _PLE_PREFETCH_BATCH_ENV = "VLLM_PLE_PREFETCH_BATCH"  # tokens per advise batch
 
 
@@ -682,6 +684,7 @@
